WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.925
In the land of Asia.

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:11.052
Welcome to Feathered Friends and Flight.
My name is Corey.

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:12.429
And I'm Katie.

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:13.805
All right, Logan, are you ready?

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:15.515
Okay, here we go.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.101
You got this?

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.355
Logan the raven gets ready

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.900
for his big performance.

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:28.278
He comes out
and it's the opening of the show.

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:33.575
Oh. And he finds a water bottle

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:39.247
that was accidentally left on the stage.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:41.541
And it's

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.128
going straight to the cam,

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:47.380
and he brings it over to the recycle bin.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.299
He puts it in the bin, recycles it.

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:52.302
Yes, he got it. Good.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:55.346
And that starts the show.

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:58.266
Why are you so good?

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.435
Good job, Roseanne.

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:03.229
You're so good.

00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:07.650
We really like to feature
natural behaviors of birds

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:12.697
and hopefully inspire the audience
for caring conservation action.

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:20.830
They can see birds
from all over the world.

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:24.959
Logan definitely
thinks he's the star of the show.

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:27.879
You can tell he's extremely handsome

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:31.424
and he always gets really great reactions

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.302
from the crowd.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:36.971
They're so smart.

00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:41.810
They've done some research that shows
that Ravens actually plan for the future.

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:45.188
They're really good at problem
solving and tool use,

00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:48.108
which is pretty amazing.

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:54.030
Logan's intelligence
keeps the team on their toes.

00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:56.616
We just need a little more depth
in this routine.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:01.412
Logan's always hungry for a challenge,
so they've come up with a new one.

00:02:01.746 --> 00:02:04.165
He's going to learn how to untie knots,

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:07.085
starting with trainer Corey shoe laces.

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:09.254
He's never done anything with shoes yet.

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:10.547
No. Okay.

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:12.590
It's a really fun behavior
with a really smart bird

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:14.968
who I think is going to get this
pretty quick. But you never know.

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:17.929
Every bird is an individual,
so we'll have to see how Logan does.

00:02:18.888 --> 00:02:21.724
All right, here comes Logan.

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:26.104
Okay, I'm going to spin them around here.

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:27.522
Just set them down on the ground.

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:29.524
Ready? Yep.

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:36.823
Good, good.

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:39.701
This is a fun puzzle.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.912
You give them a puzzle
and they figure it out immediately.

00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:45.373
Good.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:46.958
That was great.

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:49.711
Logan nails it without breaking a sweat.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.505
Thanks to a familiar technique.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.090
Katie saying good.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:57.552
He knows that good word
has been paired with food

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.679
so that he can know
he did the right thing.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.140
And if he comes back to Katie, he's
going to get a treat.

00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:06.311
That's the way

00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:09.606
you feel that when you learn something new
and you're like, I just did that thing.

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:10.940
Wow, how cool is that?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.694
It's such a good job that the birds
must have that same feeling.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.404
Out in the wild.

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:17.947
They got to use their intelligence.

00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:20.742
There are crows that have been seen
dropping things like nuts

00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:24.704
with a really strong shell onto crosswalks
so that the cars will break them open

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:25.538
for them.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.748
So they're very, very smart.

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:28.875
It's how they go
through their entire world.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.419
He did awesome.
That was like it was really good.

00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:34.005
That first training session
couldn't have gone better.

00:03:34.005 --> 00:03:36.716
It was like he had been doing this
his whole life already.

00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:39.552
But it doesn't just stop at the shoelace.

00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:42.305
There is a second part to this behavior.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.265
It's pretty complex.

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:47.018
I hope Logan's ready.

